      "mentions": 37,
      "title": {
        "en": "Caring doctors alongside communication friction"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Client feedback regarding clinic personnel presents a contrast between in-person veterinary care and front-desk coordination. Many pet owners commend compassionate doctors and attentive technicians for thorough physical exams and gentle reassurance. However, critical reviewers report abrupt phone interactions, rigid adherence to administrative policies, and pressure regarding elective procedures."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "communication",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 25,
      "title": {
        "en": "Digital coordination with phone service friction"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Communication practices generate mixed assessments across client experiences. Pet parents praise the mobile application for seamless appointment booking, medical history access, and timely clinical notes. Conversely, critical reviews describe communication challenges with front-desk dispatchers, quoting misunderstandings over the phone, and difficulties obtaining immediate clarification."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 25,
      "title": {
        "en": "Patient and comforting pet care"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet parents regularly commend the clinic's gentle and considerate approach toward dogs and cats. Reviews describe clinicians taking time to ease nervousness with treats and affectionate attention before beginning physical examinations. Several owners highlight how relaxed their pets remained during diagnostics, affirming a welcoming and secure environment for companion animals."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
